<title>MEXICO: Mexico current account surplus $641 million in Q2.</title>
<headline>Mexico current account surplus $641 million in Q2.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico notched up a current account surplus of $641 million in the second quarter compared with a surplus of $441 million in the same period in 1995, Banco de Mexico said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The central bank said the surplus was $523 million in the first six months, compared with a deficit of $751 million in the first half of last year.  </p>
<p>It said the Q2 surplus was comprised of surpluses in the trade balance, non-factor services and transfers, of $2.185 billion, $286 million and $1.218 billion respectively.</p>
<p>On the negative side, factor services showed a deficit of $3.048 billion.  </p>
<p>The following table details the current account balance of payments. All figures are in billions of dollars:</p>
<p>				     1995			1996</p>
<p>			     Q1     Q2     1H	Q1     Q2     1H</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Overall Balance   -1.192 +0.441 -0.751   -0.118 +0.841 +0.523</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Trade Balance     +0.597 +2.599 +3.196   +1.942 +2.185 +4.127</p>
<p>	Exports	   18.787 19.632 38.419   21.877 23.591 45.468</p>
<p>	Imports	   18.190 17.033 35.223   19.935 21.406 41.341</p>
<p>    Non-factor Svcs   +0.456 +0.379 +0.835   +0.603 +0.286 +0.889</p>
<p>    Factor Services   -3.119 -3.620 -6.739   -3.661 -3.048 -6.709</p>
<p>    Transfers	   +0.874 +1.083 +1.957   +0.998 +1.218 +2.216</p>
<p>-- Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9560</p>
